Aerie-Purpose: Show and hide the Aerie sidebar with Ctrl+S and resize it by drag or keys, with its width kept in aerie.sidebar.width.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui (browser_command_controller.cc, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/ui/tabs (vertical_tab_strip_state*, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/ui/views/frame (vertical_tab_strip_region_view.*, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #177. Builds on 0024. While the layout is the sidebar:

- IDC_CTRL_S_SHORTCUT flips aerie.sidebar.visible (aerie_sidebar::ToggleVisible) and does not
  collapse the strip or save the page. The region view watches the pref, slides its layer with
  AnimateLayer (transform and opacity only; opacity only under reduced motion) and takes no room
  in the window layout while it is hidden.
- The state controller never collapses, has no expand on hover, and reads and writes the width
  through aerie.sidebar.width (clamped to 200..400) instead of what a window restored.
- The width constants of Helium's strip become 260 default and 200 minimum.
- The resize area is a "Resize sidebar" splitter. A drag has no snap points and no collapse. Left and
  Right move it 10 px (aerie_sidebar::kKeyboardResizeStep), and the new width is announced.

